/T (Unlike traditional quiz events, college-level quizzing promotes presence of mind and the ability to work out answers from the questions themselves, rather than relying solely on memorized or obscure knowledge. Designed for students from classes 8th to 12th, the questions are designed to reward curiosity, presence of mind, lateral thinking, and the ability to connect seemingly unrelated pieces of information. The questions focus on current events, interesting trivia, and unexpected connections that encourage teams to logically work through and guess at answers.  )
/E (Unlike traditional quiz events, college-level quizzing promotes presence of mind and the ability to work out answers from the questions themselves, rather than relying solely on memorized or obscure knowledge. Designed for students from classes 8th to 12th, the questions are designed to reward curiosity, presence of mind, lateral thinking, and the ability to connect seemingly unrelated pieces of information. The questions focus on current events, interesting trivia, and unexpected connections that encourage teams to logically work through and guess at answers.  )
